<div class="span9 about-main-image">
<div class="span6 about-description"><h1 class="sr-only">RFPs / RFQs / RFEIs</h1>
<p>Consult this page to learn more about development opportunities on public sites, and see below the open Requests for Proposals (RFPs), Requests for Qualifications (RFQs), and Requests for Expressions of Interest (RFEIs).</p>
<div class="row">
<div class="span6"><a href="https://www1.nyc.gov/site/hpd/about/hpd-newsletter-sign-up.page" class="button-link btn-standard-hpd">Sign up for Email Alerts</a></div>
<div class="span6">&nbsp;</div>
</div>
<p>
<script type="text/javascript" src="/assets/home/js/pages/agencies/expand-collapse-2.js"></script>
</p>
<div class="faq-v1">
<div class="faq-head">
<h2 class="faq-heading">Open Requests</h2>
<div class="faq-controls"><a href="javascript:expandAll();" class="faq-expand-all">Expand All</a><a href="javascript:collapseAll();" class="faq-collapse-all">Collapse All</a></div>
</div>
<p class="sr-only">Click a topic, or press the enter key on a topic, to reveal its answer.</p>
<div data-answer="faq1b" class="faq-questions">
<p>ANCP, TPT-TP &amp; Special Projects RFP</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq1b">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/ancp-tpt-tp-special-projects-rfq.page">ANCP, TPT-TP &amp; Special Projects RFP</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: rolling</em></p>
<p>This RFQ is for qualified not-for-profit and for-profit organizations to participate in the rehabilitation and management of multifamily residential properties through HPD's Affordable Neighborhood Cooperative Program, Third Party Transfer &ndash; Tenant Petition Cooperatives, and other Special Projects. HPD invites qualified individuals and organizations to submit descriptions of their qualifications to rehabilitate and create affordable cooperatives through these programs.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq1d" class="faq-questions">
<p>Monitor of Housing Development Fund Corporation Cooperatives RFQ</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq1d">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/coop-monitor-rfq.page">Monitor of Housing Development Fund Corporation Cooperatives RFQ</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: August 14, 2024 for inclusion in initial pre-qualified list; rolling thereafter.</em></p>
<p>Through this Request for Qualifications (RFQ), HPD aims to establish a pre-qualified list of organizations who may provide monitoring services to Housing Development Fund Corporation Cooperatives. Not-for-profit and for-profit organizations qualified as &ldquo;Coop Monitors&rdquo; via this RFQ will provide crucial technical assistance to ensure the stability and longevity of HDFC coops operating across the city.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq2" class="faq-questions">
<p>HomeFirst RFQ</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq2">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/homefirst-rfq.page">HomeFirst RFQ</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: 9/22/2023</em></p>
<p>HPD is inviting non-profit organizations with experience managing affordable homeownership programs in the City for a government agency or other public sector entity, to submit qualifications demonstrating their interest and ability to perform the activities related to the HPD's HomeFirst Down Payment Assistance Program.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq2a" class="faq-questions">
<p>HPD Family Living Center Services RFP</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq2a">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/hpd-family-living-center-services-rfp.page">HPD Family Living Center Services RFP</a><br /><em>Submission Deadline: Friday, December 27,, 2024 at 2:00pm</em></p>
<p>HPD anticipates awarding a minimum of three contracts across the boroughs of Manhattan, Brooklyn, and the Bronx for Family Living Centers that shelter households displaced by a City issued vacate order. Proposals for each borough must be submitted separately. HPD will assign relocatees to specific Family Living Center sites based on the availability of appropriately sized units for the household and the proximity of the facility to the relocatee&rsquo;s former residence and/or any special needs accommodations.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq2b" class="faq-questions">
<p>HPD Housing Ambassador Services RFEI: FY2027</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq2b">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/housing-ambassador-services-rfei.page">HPD Housing Ambassador Services RFEI: FY2027</a><br /></p>
<p><em><strong>Submission Deadline: </strong>Friday, August 21st, 2026, at 2:00 PM</em></p>
<p>The Department of Housing Preservation and Development (&ldquo;HPD&rdquo;) is seeking qualified community-based organizations (&ldquo;CBOs&rdquo;) to submit a response to the Request for Expressions of Interest (&ldquo;RFEI&rdquo;) for providing education and services to assist affordable housing seekers in preparing and applying for housing, as well as in providing information to clients about free &ldquo;Ready to Rent&rdquo; financial counseling services available through the City Council-designated financial counseling provider, Ariva.</p>
<p>This funding supports the &ldquo;Ready to Rent&rdquo; program, which is an inter-agency initiative managed by HPD and the NYC Department of Consumer and Worker Protection (DCWP). A central component of this program is to support and expand the capacity of housing organizations and community social service providers (&ldquo;Housing Ambassadors&rdquo;), which is critical to the success of the New Yorkers looking for affordable housing.&nbsp;</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq2c" class="faq-questions">
<p>Hunter&rsquo;s Point South Parcel E RFP</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq2c">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/hunterspointe-rfp.page">Hunter&rsquo;s Point South Parcel E RFP</a><br /><em>Submission: 09/05/2025</em></p>
<p>The NYC Department of Housing Preservation and Development (HPD) is accepting proposals to develop a mixed-use project with affordable housing and community amenities on a City-owned lot in Hunter&rsquo;s Point South, Queens..</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq3" class="faq-questions">
<p>Inclusionary Housing Program Administering Agent RFQ</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq3">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/inclusionary-housing-administering-agent-rfq.page">Inclusionary Housing Program Administering Agent RFQ</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: rolling</em></p>
<p>HPD is seeking qualified not-for-profit organizations to submit RFQs for the provision of services by an Inclusionary Housing Program Administering Agent.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq4" class="faq-questions">
<p>Mitchell-Lama Property Management RFQ</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq4">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/mitchell-lama-property-management-rfq.page">Mitchell-Lama Property Management RFQ</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: rolling</em></p>
<p>HPD is seeking to identify applicants for consideration as property managers to assume property management responsibilities for Mitchell-Lama developments in HPD's Division of Housing Supervision's portfolio.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="mimi" class="faq-questions">
<p>Mixed Income Market Initiative RFEI</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="mimi">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/mimi-rfei.page">Mixed Income Market Initiative RFEI</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: February 15, 2024</em></p>
<p>This RFQ is for qualified not-for-profit and for-profit organizations to develop mixed income housing projects within the five boroughs. HPD invites qualified organizations to apply per the instructions in the RFEI.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq4b" class="faq-questions">
<p>Moving On RFP Re-Solicitation</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq4b">
<p><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/moving-on-rfp.page">Moving On RFP Re-Solicitation</a><br /><em>Re-Solicitation RFP Submission deadline: 03/29/2024</em><br /><em>Original Re-Solicitation RFP Submission deadline: 03/26/2024</em><br /><em>Original RFP Submission deadline: 10/31/2023</em></p>
<p>HPD seeks the services of a qualified Contractor to expand implementation of Moving On, an existing City program that assists individuals who have stabilized while living in supportive housing and no longer need or want intensive, on-site support to become more self-sufficient and move to independent housing. The program supports tenants throughout the entire move process including providing access to tenant based rental assistance. With a focus on program expansion, capacity building and subcontractor training and financial management, the selected Contractor will provide program informed training, technical assistance and financial administration services that include screening interested not-for-profit agencies that operate permanent supportive housing, on-boarding training cohorts, developing and delivering a training curriculum, and tracking outcomes.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq5" class="faq-questions">
<p>Neighborhood Builders Fast Track RFQ and RFPs</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq5">
<p><strong>Neighborhood Builders Fast Track RFQ and RFPs</strong> <br /><br /></p>
<p>The NYC Department of Housing Preservation and Development (HPD) has established a new pipeline of simpler, faster-to-develop sites to be released to qualified non-profit organizations and minority or women-owned (M/WBE) developers to build new affordable housing.</p>
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/neighborhood-builders-rfps.page">Neighborhood Builders Fast Track &ndash; RFPs</a></p>
<ul>
<li>Learn more about the Neighborhood Builders process and RFQs</li>
</ul>
<p><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/neighborhood-builders-rfq.page">Neighborhood Builders Fast Track &ndash; RFQ</a></p>
<ul>
<li>Apply to become a prequalified nonprofit or M/WBE developer</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq5a" class="faq-questions">
<p>New Utrecht Library and Affordable Housing RFP</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq5a">
<p><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/new-utrecht-library-rfp.page">New Utrecht Library and Affordable Housing RFP</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: 09/04/2026</em></p>
<p>The NYC Department of Housing Preservation and Development (HPD and Brooklyn Public Library (BPL) are accepting proposals for the redevelopment of New Utrecht Library in Brooklyn with a new state-of-the-art library alongside 100 percent affordable housing.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq5b" class="faq-questions">
<p>NYC 15/15 Rental Assistance RFP</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq5b">
<p><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/nyc-15-15-rental-assistance-rfp.page">NYC 15/15 Rental Assistance RFP</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: July 20, 2026</em></p>
<p>HPD's Office of Housing Access and Stability is accepting proposals from owners of supportive housing projects with New York City-administered service contracts who are interested in project-based rental assistance. Supportive housing projects eligible for this RFP must be preserving or rehabilitating existing supportive housing units. NYC 15/15 Rental Assistance is project-based rental assistance awarded for an initial term of up to 15 years. HPD will award rental assistance to up to 150 units across all projects in this cycle of the competitive selection process.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq5c" class="faq-questions">
<p>Planning and Development Resources RFQ</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq5c">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/planning-and-development-resources-rfq.page">Planning and Development Resources RFQ</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: rolling</em></p>
<p>HPD regularly receives inquiries from non-profits, faith-based organizations, and other private owners who have developable land and a mission-driven interest in providing affordable housing and community facilities, but who lack the required real estate development experience to carry through a deal. Through the Planning and Development Resources RFQ, HPD seeks to provide a list of qualified consultants who can guide such owners through the pre-development and/or construction phases to develop or preserve high-quality, affordable housing or mixed-use projects on their sites.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq6" class="faq-questions">
<p>Preservation Buyer RFQ</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq6">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/preservation-buyer-rfq.page">Preservation Buyer RFQ</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: rolling</em></p>
<p>The objective of this RFQ is to create a resource so that HPD may refer prospective sellers of property, community-based organizations, and others as deemed appropriate to the Qualified List when seeking a Qualified Preservation Buyer who will purchase the property and extend any underlying affordability restrictions.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq8aa" class="faq-questions">
<p>Property Pathways RFEI</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq8aa">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/property-pathways-rfei.page">Property Pathways RFEI</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: rolling</em></p>
<p>This RFEI is for proposals identifying existing vacant or partially vacant buildings in order to provide affordable permanent housing for formerly homeless and other rent-burdened households.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq8b" class="faq-questions">
<p>Qualified Marketing Agent RFQ</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq8b">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/marketing-agent-rfq.page">Qualified Marketing Agent RFQ</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: rolling</em></p>
<p>HPD and HDC are seeking to identify entities for consideration as Qualified Marketing Agents to assume the marketing, lease-up, and sales responsibilities for City-sponsored affordable housing in HPD and/or HDC's Marketing Affordability and Oversight Units' portfolio.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq1aabb" class="faq-questions">
<p>Supportive Housing RFQ</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq1aabb">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/supportive-housing-rfq.page">Supportive Housing RFQ</a><br /><em>Initial submission deadline: 06/15/2023</em></p>
<p>HPD seeks to establish a list of Qualified Supportive Housing Developers (Qualified List) that HPD designates as qualified to develop and construct high-quality supportive housing development projects on sites that will be available for disposition by HPD or other City agency.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-v1">
<div class="faq-head">
<h2 class="faq-heading">Submissions Under Review</h2>
<div class="faq-controls"><a href="javascript:expandAll();" class="faq-expand-all">Expand All</a><a href="javascript:collapseAll();" class="faq-collapse-all">Collapse All</a></div>
</div>
<p class="sr-only">Click a topic, or press the enter key on a topic, to reveal its answer.</p>
<div data-answer="faq1aa" class="faq-questions">
<p>Edgemere CLT RFEI</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq1aa">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/edgemere-clt-rfei.page">Edgemere CLT RFEI</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: September 24, 2021 (updated from September 10, 2021)</em></p>
<p>The Edgemere Community Land Trust (CLT) Request for Expressions of Interest (RFEI) jumpstarts the community's vision for a local community land trust partner able to develop affordable homeownership opportunities and provide for neighborhood management of public open space and resilient land activities.</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq1ac">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/housing-ambassador-services-rfei.page">Housing Ambassador Services RFEI</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: Thursday, August 29th, 2024 at 2:00pm</em></p>
<p>HPD is seeking qualified community-based organizations to submit a response to the Request for Expressions of Interest (RFEI) for providing education and services to assist affordable housing seekers in preparing and applying for housing, as well as in providing information to clients about free &ldquo;Ready to Rent&rdquo; financial counseling services available through the City Council-designated financial counseling provider, Ariva.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq1f" class="faq-questions">
<p>Housing Retention and Stabilization Services RFQ</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq1f">
<p><a href="https://www.nyc.gov/site/hpd/services-and-information/updated-housing-retention-stabilization-services-rfq.page"><strong>Housing Retention Stabilization Services RFQ</strong></a><br /><em>Release date:Release date: October 17, 2023&nbsp;</em><br />Submission deadline: <em>Rolling</em></p>
<p><span>Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis and evaluated periodically. HPD maintain a list of qualified Housing Retention and Stabilization Services providers to assist formerly homeless and low-income households in HPD-assisted new construction and preservation</span>&nbsp;projects.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq10a" class="faq-questions">
<p>NYCHA NextGen Neighborhoods - La Guardia Houses RFP</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq10a">
<p><strong>NYCHA NextGen Neighborhoods - La Guardia Houses RFP</strong><br /><em>Release date: 03/01/2018<br />Submission deadline: 06/01/2018</em></p>
<p>NYCHA and HPD are currently reviewing&nbsp;proposals for the development of mixed-income housing at La Guardia Houses. The RFP is the outcome of extensive resident and community stakeholder engagement as part of NYCHA's NextGen Neighborhoods program, which will generate revenue to be reinvested back into the development sites and across NYCHA's portfolio by leveraging a 50-50 split of market-rate and affordable housing units.</p>
<p>The La Guardia Houses RFP is informed by a significant planning and engagement process with NYCHA residents that began in April 2017 and that will continue through developer selection, pre-development, construction and leasing. The project described throughout this RFP reflects the community needs and neighborhood goals NYCHA heard repeatedly in community outreach and canvassing, community visioning workshops, and NYCHA resident engagement meetings. The recommendations identified through this engagement process are captured in the Community Visioning document.</p>
<p>The RFP development site is located on the La Guardia Houses NYCHA campus in Manhattan Community District 3. The development site is approximately 18,000 square feet and bounded by Madison Street, the NYCHA campus and the Little Flower Playground.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq12" class="faq-questions">
<p>NextGeneration NYCHA - 100% Affordable Housing Development Sites RFP</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq12">
<p><strong>NextGeneration NYCHA - 100% Affordable Housing Development Sites RFP</strong><br /><em>Release date: 06/01/2017<br />Submission deadline: 08/11/2017</em></p>
<p>NYCHA and HPD are currently reviewing proposals from a Prequalified List (PQL) for NYCHA's 100 Percent Affordable program for Site 4.</p>
<p>Site 4 - Harbor View Terrace, is a parcel (portion of Block 1084, Lot 9) of NYCHA-owned land bounded by West 55th Street, NYCHA's Harborview Terrace Building, West 56th Street, and a six-story commercial building. The goal for Harborview Terrace is to build affordable housing for families.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq8b" class="faq-questions">
<p>Project-Based Vouchers RFP</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq8b">
<p><strong>Project-Based Vouchers RFP</strong></p>
<p>The City of New York Department of Housing Preservation and Development (HPD), Division of Tenant Resources, is reviewing submissions for the awarding of Section 8 <a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/project-based-vouchers-rfp.page">Project Based Vouchers</a> (PBVs).</p>
<p>The use of federally-funded Project Based Vouchers is subject to the regulations set forth in 24 CFR 983, as well as the Project Based Housing Assistance Payment Contract (HUD Form HUD 52530B). This RFP is for &ldquo;newly constructed housing&rdquo; and &ldquo;existing housing&rdquo; &nbsp;as defined under 24 CFR 983.3 (b).</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq13" class="faq-questions">
<p>Primary Prevention Program RFQ</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq13">
<p><strong>Primary Prevention Program RFQ</strong><br /><em>Release date: 02/24/2017<br />Submission deadline: 03/09/2017</em></p>
<p>HPD is currently reviewing submissions in response to the Notice of Funding Availability (NOFA) for the Lead Hazard Reduction Demonstration Grant of 2017 by the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD). The grant provides funding of HPD's Primary Prevention Program (PPP). PPP offers federally funded grants for lead treatment to owners of single and multifamily buildings constructed prior to 1960.</p>
<p>HPD intends to respond to the grant and will work with Community Based Organization(s) to undertake outreach to local building owners and residents in specific neighborhoods in the Bronx, Brooklyn, and Queens, listed in the RFQ.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq15" class="faq-questions">
<p>Sea View Healthy Community RFEI</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq15">
<p><strong><a href="https://edc.nyc/project/sea-view-healthy-community">Sea View Healthy Community RFEI</a></strong></p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq15a" class="faq-questions">
<p>Security Deposit Alternatives RFEI</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq15a">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/security-deposit-rfei.page">Security Deposit Alternatives RFEI</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: 9/15/2023</em></p>
<p>HPD and HDC are seeking to identify entities for consideration as Security Deposit Alternative Providers to offer their alternatives to renters leasing newly-constructed City- and/or HDC-sponsored affordable housing. These Products are financial services that allow renters to pay a portion of their security deposit value instead of the full amount at the time of lease-up.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq3bcb" class="faq-questions">
<p>Shared Equity RFI</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq3bcb">
<p><a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/shared-equity-rfi.page">Shared Equity RFI</a><br /><em>Submission deadline: 7/9/2021</em></p>
<p>The City is reviewing responses and anticipates releasing a subsequent Request for Expressions of Interest (RFEI) or Request for Proposal (RFP) for shared equity projects, incorporating information gathered through the Shared Equity RFI.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq16" class="faq-questions">
<p>Small Projects Contractor RFQ</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq16">
<p><strong>Small Projects Contractor RFQ</strong><br /><em>Release date: 12/19/2018<br />Submission deadline: 02/06/2019</em></p>
<p>HPD requested Statements of Qualification from contractors to perform moderate rehabilitation of affordable housing projects financed by HPD for scopes of work totaling less than $1 million. HPD is prequalifying firms to support small and mid-sized building owners (3-50 units) and low-cost projects to successfully implement needed rehabilitation and energy efficiency work. HPD is particularly looking to support small building owners (between 3-15 units), and expects the bulk of projects that will use the list of prequalified firms to bid out scopes that typically consist of the replacement of 3-4 building systems (i.e. boiler, windows, roof, electrical, fa&ccedil;ade, plumbing) and total less than $500,000. The objective of this effort is to broaden the pool of qualified firms to work on HPD-financed projects and streamline the building owners' contract and bidding process for smaller moderate rehabilitation projects that HPD finances.</p>
</div>
<div data-answer="faq17" class="faq-questions">
<p>Third Party Transfer Program Round X, Multifamily Preservation Loan Program RFQ</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-answers" id="faq17">
<p><strong>Third Party Transfer Program Round X, Multifamily Preservation Loan Program RFQ</strong><br /><em>Release date: 03/13/2017<br />Submission deadline: 04/24/2017</em></p>
<p>HPD is currently reviewing submissions for the rehabilitation and management of multifamily residential properties through the agency's Third Party Transfer (TPT) Program, Multifamily Preservation Loan Program (MPLP), and Rental Special Project.</p>
<p>HPD expects to qualify more potential developers than available properties. Therefore, some qualified developers will not be selected. HPD reserves the right to negotiate with any number of qualified developers, accept or reject any or all applications received as a result of the RFQ, or postpone or cancel the RFQ in part or in its entirety.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h3>Designated Requests</h3>
<p>Search HPD's <a href="/site/hpd/services-and-information/designated-rfp-projects.page">Designated Requests</a> archive.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
